{"action": "setfields", "pairs": [{"label": "put your pm hat", "value": "At Thryv I built an AI code reviewer for the whole org, and the hardest part was not the engineering - it was the product call. The obvious version auto-posts every AI finding on every pull request, but I had seen that pattern erode trust: reviewers quickly start ignoring a bot that is noisy or occasionally wrong. So I reframed the problem from 'how do we automate review' to 'how do we save review time without spending reviewer trust.' I scoped it deliberately - the tool ranks findings by severity and confidence, then stages only the top few as draft comments for a human to approve before anything is posted. That tradeoff, less automation in exchange for more trust, is exactly what got it adopted across teams instead of muted. It reminded me that a complex product problem is usually a question of what NOT to build."}], "tabId": 1232840932, "status": "delivered", "queued": "2026-07-22"}
